% 2-cycle-plus-spare pattern AGAINST the hexagon condition.
% Same ground hypotheses as square.in (a1 |><| b2, a2 |><| b1, (H1), (H2), cw != cz,
% general position), plus the matching-pattern condition as a universal clause.
% Any model is a finite projection algebra satisfying the hexagon condition in which
% the 2-cycle-plus-spare pattern fails, i.e. a genuine separation (the case not
% covered by Prop. 4.10 of the notes).  No model up to size n = evidence that the
% pattern follows from the hexagon condition for finite algebras.
%
% The universal clause used is the TRIANGLE condition (14 literals): on finite
% algebras it is equivalent to the hexagon condition (Theorem 4.8), and it is
% cheaper for Mace4 than the 20-literal hexagon clause (given below, commented out).
%   x * y = y x y  (= x theta_y).  Constants: a1,a2,a3,b1,b2,b3,cw,cz.

op(400, infix, "*").

formulas(assumptions).
x * x = x.
(y * x) * x = y * x.
(x * y) * x = y * x.
((z * x) * y) * x = z * (y * x).
(((z * x) * y) * x) * y = (z * x) * y.

a1 * a2 = cw.   a2 * a3 = cw.   a3 * a1 = cw.
b1 * b2 = cz.   b2 * b3 = cz.   b3 * b1 = cz.
a1 * b1 = b1 * a1.   a2 * b2 = b2 * a2.   a3 * b3 = b3 * a3.
b2 * a1 = a1.   a1 * b2 = b2.
b1 * a2 = a2.   a2 * b1 = b1.
cw != cz.

% general position: none of the four free pairs (a1,b3), (a2,b3), (a3,b1), (a3,b2) is matched
% (a pair p,q is matched iff q*p = p and p*q = q; so 'not matched' is a disjunction).
% Delete these four lines for the raw search (expect P(Q_0)-based models of size 11, 12 first).
b3 * a1 != a1 | a1 * b3 != b3.
b3 * a2 != a2 | a2 * b3 != b3.
b1 * a3 != a3 | a3 * b1 != b1.
b2 * a3 != a3 | a3 * b2 != b2.

% ---- triangle condition (x_i |><| y_{i+1}), positive form, w and z eliminated ----
x1 * x2 != x2 * x3 |
x1 * x2 != x3 * x1 |
y1 * y2 != y2 * y3 |
y1 * y2 != y3 * y1 |
x1 * y1 != y1 * x1 |
x2 * y2 != y2 * x2 |
x3 * y3 != y3 * x3 |
y2 * x1 != x1 |
x1 * y2 != y2 |
y3 * x2 != x2 |
x2 * y3 != y3 |
y1 * x3 != x3 |
x3 * y1 != y1 |
x1 * x2 = y1 * y2.

% ---- alternative: hexagon condition (all six pairs matched), 20 literals ----
% x1 * x2 != x2 * x3 |
% x1 * x2 != x3 * x1 |
% y1 * y2 != y2 * y3 |
% y1 * y2 != y3 * y1 |
% x1 * y1 != y1 * x1 |
% x2 * y2 != y2 * x2 |
% x3 * y3 != y3 * x3 |
% y2 * x1 != x1 |
% x1 * y2 != y2 |
% y3 * x1 != x1 |
% x1 * y3 != y3 |
% y1 * x2 != x2 |
% x2 * y1 != y1 |
% y3 * x2 != x2 |
% x2 * y3 != y3 |
% y1 * x3 != x3 |
% x3 * y1 != y1 |
% y2 * x3 != x3 |
% x3 * y2 != y2 |
% x1 * x2 = y1 * y2.
end_of_list.
